              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Temporary storage entries are removed when their TTL lapses, so data written there can silently disappear. Keys that look like configuration, balances, or ownership are strong hints that the value is meant to persist. This is a key-name heuristic and reports low confidence."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Durable data written to temporary storage\n\nTemporary storage entries are removed when their TTL lapses, so data written there can silently disappear. Keys that look like configuration, balances, or ownership are strong hints that the value is meant to persist. This is a key-name heuristic and reports low confidence.\n\n### Remediation\n\nWrite durable state to persistent (or instance) storage. Use temporary storage only for data that may safely be discarded, and extend its TTL when it is still needed.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/state-archival",
                "text": "Temporary storage entries are removed when their TTL lapses, so data written there can silently disappear. Keys that look like configuration, balances, or ownership are strong hints that the value is meant to persist. This is a key-name heuristic and reports low confidence.\n\nRemediation: Write durable state to persistent (or instance) storage. Use temporary storage only for data that may safely be discarded, and extend its TTL when it is still needed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data",
              "id": "SS-021",
              "name": "Durable data written to temporary storage",
              "properties": {
