              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract uses `symbol_short!` with a literal longer than the nine-character short-symbol limit, or builds the symbol from caller-controlled input. Overlong literals do not describe the symbol the author expects once truncated or fail to compile, while caller-built short symbols can deliberately collide with another key and overwrite or misread storage. This is a syntactic heuristic and reports medium confidence."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Unsafe symbol_short key\n\nA contract uses `symbol_short!` with a literal longer than the nine-character short-symbol limit, or builds the symbol from caller-controlled input. Overlong literals do not describe the symbol the author expects once truncated or fail to compile, while caller-built short symbols can deliberately collide with another key and overwrite or misread storage. This is a syntactic heuristic and reports medium confidence.\n\n### Remediation\n\nUse a constant literal of at most nine characters such as `symbol_short!(\"transfer\")`, or use `Symbol::new(&env, value)` for longer or dynamic values. Never derive a storage key directly from caller input; map it through an allowlist of known keys.\n\n### References\n\n- https://docs.rs/soroban-sdk/latest/soroban_sdk/macro.symbol_short.html\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A contract uses `symbol_short!` with a literal longer than the nine-character short-symbol limit, or builds the symbol from caller-controlled input. Overlong literals do not describe the symbol the author expects once truncated or fail to compile, while caller-built short symbols can deliberately collide with another key and overwrite or misread storage. This is a syntactic heuristic and reports medium confidence.\n\nRemediation: Use a constant literal of at most nine characters such as `symbol_short!(\"transfer\")`, or use `Symbol::new(&env, value)` for longer or dynamic values. Never derive a storage key directly from caller input; map it through an allowlist of known keys."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.rs/soroban-sdk/latest/soroban_sdk/macro.symbol_short.html",
              "id": "SS-022",
              "name": "Unsafe symbol_short key",
              "properties": {
