              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Events are public on the ledger forever. Publishing a value whose name suggests a secret (secret, key, seed, proof) risks an irreversible disclosure. This is a name-based heuristic over parameters and string literals and reports low confidence."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Sensitive-looking data published in events\n\nEvents are public on the ledger forever. Publishing a value whose name suggests a secret (secret, key, seed, proof) risks an irreversible disclosure. This is a name-based heuristic over parameters and string literals and reports low confidence.\n\n### Remediation\n\nDo not publish secrets or secret-derived values in events. Commit to a hash if you must prove knowledge, and keep key material, seeds, and preimages off-chain.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/events\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "Events are public on the ledger forever. Publishing a value whose name suggests a secret (secret, key, seed, proof) risks an irreversible disclosure. This is a name-based heuristic over parameters and string literals and reports low confidence.\n\nRemediation: Do not publish secrets or secret-derived values in events. Commit to a hash if you must prove knowledge, and keep key material, seeds, and preimages off-chain."
              },
