            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A public entry point makes a cross-contract call and then mutates storage without a visible reentrancy guard. Soroban permits reentrancy, so a malicious callee can re-enter while state is inconsistent. The detector recognizes a documented guard pattern: a storage flag with a lock/guard-style key is read and set before the call."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Cross-contract call without a reentrancy guard\n\nA public entry point makes a cross-contract call and then mutates storage without a visible reentrancy guard. Soroban permits reentrancy, so a malicious callee can re-enter while state is inconsistent. The detector recognizes a documented guard pattern: a storage flag with a lock/guard-style key is read and set before the call.\n\n### Remediation\n\nBefore the external call, read a lock flag from storage, reject when it is already set, and set it; clear it after the state update. Or follow checks-effects-interactions and update all state before calling out.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs",
                "text": "A public entry point makes a cross-contract call and then mutates storage without a visible reentrancy guard. Soroban permits reentrancy, so a malicious callee can re-enter while state is inconsistent. The detector recognizes a documented guard pattern: a storage flag with a lock/guard-style key is read and set before the call.\n\nRemediation: Before the external call, read a lock flag from storage, reject when it is already set, and set it; clear it after the state update. Or follow checks-effects-interactions and update all state before calling out."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
