              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A `token::Client` is constructed from a caller-supplied address without comparing it to configuration stored by the contract. An attacker can substitute a malicious token contract and change balances or transfer semantics. The detector looks for a storage read and comparison that guards the construction."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Token client built from an unvalidated caller address\n\nA `token::Client` is constructed from a caller-supplied address without comparing it to configuration stored by the contract. An attacker can substitute a malicious token contract and change balances or transfer semantics. The detector looks for a storage read and comparison that guards the construction.\n\n### Remediation\n\nCompare the supplied token address with the address stored when the contract was configured, and reject mismatches with a typed error before constructing the client.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/tokens/token-interface\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A `token::Client` is constructed from a caller-supplied address without comparing it to configuration stored by the contract. An attacker can substitute a malicious token contract and change balances or transfer semantics. The detector looks for a storage read and comparison that guards the construction.\n\nRemediation: Compare the supplied token address with the address stored when the contract was configured, and reject mismatches with a typed error before constructing the client."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/tokens/token-interface",
