              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A source file imports everything from `soroban_sdk` with a glob (`use soroban_sdk::*;` or a nested glob). Wildcard imports obscure which SDK items are used and can silently include deprecated or unsafe APIs when the SDK changes. This is a readability and reviewability signal, not proof of a security defect."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Wildcard import from the Soroban SDK\n\nA source file imports everything from `soroban_sdk` with a glob (`use soroban_sdk::*;` or a nested glob). Wildcard imports obscure which SDK items are used and can silently include deprecated or unsafe APIs when the SDK changes. This is a readability and reviewability signal, not proof of a security defect.\n\n### Remediation\n\nReplace the glob with the specific `soroban_sdk` items the contract uses (for example `use soroban_sdk::{Address, Env};`). Nested module imports should likewise name each item instead of ending in `*`.\n\n### References\n\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch07-04-bringing-paths-into-scope-with-the-use-keyword.html\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs",
                "text": "A source file imports everything from `soroban_sdk` with a glob (`use soroban_sdk::*;` or a nested glob). Wildcard imports obscure which SDK items are used and can silently include deprecated or unsafe APIs when the SDK changes. This is a readability and reviewability signal, not proof of a security defect.\n\nRemediation: Replace the glob with the specific `soroban_sdk` items the contract uses (for example `use soroban_sdk::{Address, Env};`). Nested module imports should likewise name each item instead of ending in `*`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch07-04-bringing-paths-into-scope-with-the-use-keyword.html",
              "id": "SS-033",
              "name": "Wildcard import from the Soroban SDK",
              "properties": {
                "category": "dependencies",
                "confidence": "high",
                "references": [
                  "https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch07-04-bringing-paths-into-scope-with-the-use-keyword.html",
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs"
                ],
                "remediation": "Replace the glob with the specific `soroban_sdk` items the contract uses (for example `use soroban_sdk::{Address, Env};`). Nested module imports should likewise name each item instead of ending in `*`.",
                "severity": "low"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Wildcard import from the Soroban SDK"
              }
            },
