              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point uses `env.deployer()` to deploy or register a contract without any `require_auth` authorization fact in the function or its intra-file helpers. Deploying contracts is a privileged action; if it is open to any caller, an attacker can install attacker-controlled code, replace a contract, or consume the contract's deployment quota. The detector is syntactic and reports low confidence because authorization may be enforced elsewhere."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Unvalidated deployer usage\n\nA contract entry point uses `env.deployer()` to deploy or register a contract without any `require_auth` authorization fact in the function or its intra-file helpers. Deploying contracts is a privileged action; if it is open to any caller, an attacker can install attacker-controlled code, replace a contract, or consume the contract's deployment quota. The detector is syntactic and reports low confidence because authorization may be enforced elsewhere.\n\n### Remediation\n\nRequire authorization from the administrator or the address that owns the deployment before calling `env.deployer()`, for example `admin.require_auth()` after loading a trusted admin address from storage. Bind the authorization to the deployed address or salt where possible, and reject callers that are not allowed to deploy.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/guides/deploying-contracts",
                "text": "A contract entry point uses `env.deployer()` to deploy or register a contract without any `require_auth` authorization fact in the function or its intra-file helpers. Deploying contracts is a privileged action; if it is open to any caller, an attacker can install attacker-controlled code, replace a contract, or consume the contract's deployment quota. The detector is syntactic and reports low confidence because authorization may be enforced elsewhere.\n\nRemediation: Require authorization from the administrator or the address that owns the deployment before calling `env.deployer()`, for example `admin.require_auth()` after loading a trusted admin address from storage. Bind the authorization to the deployed address or salt where possible, and reject callers that are not allowed to deploy."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
              "id": "SS-034",
              "name": "Unvalidated deployer usage",
              "properties": {
                "category": "access-control",
                "confidence": "low",
                "references": [
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/guides/deploying-contracts"
                ],
                "remediation": "Require authorization from the administrator or the address that owns the deployment before calling `env.deployer()`, for example `admin.require_auth()` after loading a trusted admin address from storage. Bind the authorization to the deployed address or salt where possible, and reject callers that are not allowed to deploy.",
                "severity": "high"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unvalidated deployer usage"
              }
            },
