                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security"
                ],
                "remediation": "Prefer a single, explicit authorization for the actor whose operation this is, or bind all required parties through one documented multi-sig pattern. If the flow genuinely requires several independent approvals, document the policy and suppress the finding with a justified inline directive.",
                "severity": "medium"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Competing authorization calls"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point reads persistent storage but does not call `extend_ttl`, `set_ttl`, or `bump` in the same function or in the intra-file helpers it calls. Persistent entries expire; if the read assumes the value is still present, an expired entry can change the contract's behaviour or block an operation that depends on it. The detector reports only when no TTL management is visible at all: a TTL call for an unrelated key is treated as ambiguous and suppresses the finding."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Persistent storage read without TTL management\n\nA contract entry point reads persistent storage but does not call `extend_ttl`, `set_ttl`, or `bump` in the same function or in the intra-file helpers it calls. Persistent entries expire; if the read assumes the value is still present, an expired entry can change the contract's behaviour or block an operation that depends on it. The detector reports only when no TTL management is visible at all: a TTL call for an unrelated key is treated as ambiguous and suppresses the finding.\n\n### Remediation\n\nRefresh the entry's time-to-live when reading persistent data that must remain available, for example `env.storage().persistent().extend_ttl(&key, threshold, extend_to)` after the read. Prefer one documented TTL policy per contract. If TTL is managed by a separate maintenance entry point, suppress this rule for the reader with a justification.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data",
                "text": "A contract entry point reads persistent storage but does not call `extend_ttl`, `set_ttl`, or `bump` in the same function or in the intra-file helpers it calls. Persistent entries expire; if the read assumes the value is still present, an expired entry can change the contract's behaviour or block an operation that depends on it. The detector reports only when no TTL management is visible at all: a TTL call for an unrelated key is treated as ambiguous and suppresses the finding.\n\nRemediation: Refresh the entry's time-to-live when reading persistent data that must remain available, for example `env.storage().persistent().extend_ttl(&key, threshold, extend_to)` after the read. Prefer one documented TTL policy per contract. If TTL is managed by a separate maintenance entry point, suppress this rule for the reader with a justification."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data",
              "id": "SS-039",
              "name": "Persistent storage read without TTL management",
              "properties": {
                "category": "storage",
                "confidence": "low",
                "references": [
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data"
                ],
                "remediation": "Refresh the entry's time-to-live when reading persistent data that must remain available, for example `env.storage().persistent().extend_ttl(&key, threshold, extend_to)` after the read. Prefer one documented TTL policy per contract. If TTL is managed by a separate maintenance entry point, suppress this rule for the reader with a justification.",
                "severity": "medium"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Persistent storage read without TTL management"
              }
