              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A cross-contract token call receives an address argument that originates from a caller-supplied parameter and was not passed through a documented address-validation helper. The scanner cannot prove the address is the expected account or contract, so a caller may direct a transfer, approval, mint, or burn at an unintended destination. Flows with more than one origin, or validation that happens only on some paths, are recorded as ambiguous by the taint analysis and are not reported."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Cross-contract call with an unvalidated address argument\n\nA cross-contract token call receives an address argument that originates from a caller-supplied parameter and was not passed through a documented address-validation helper. The scanner cannot prove the address is the expected account or contract, so a caller may direct a transfer, approval, mint, or burn at an unintended destination. Flows with more than one origin, or validation that happens only on some paths, are recorded as ambiguous by the taint analysis and are not reported.\n\n### Remediation\n\nValidate the address before the cross-contract call. Use a documented helper such as `validate_address`, compare against an address stored at configuration time, or reject addresses that are not on an explicit allowlist. Validate on every path, before the call.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/tokens/token-interface",
                "text": "A cross-contract token call receives an address argument that originates from a caller-supplied parameter and was not passed through a documented address-validation helper. The scanner cannot prove the address is the expected account or contract, so a caller may direct a transfer, approval, mint, or burn at an unintended destination. Flows with more than one origin, or validation that happens only on some paths, are recorded as ambiguous by the taint analysis and are not reported.\n\nRemediation: Validate the address before the cross-contract call. Use a documented helper such as `validate_address`, compare against an address stored at configuration time, or reject addresses that are not on an explicit allowlist. Validate on every path, before the call."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
